  "answer": "Changes made (only the five writable files):\n\n- **`normalize.mjs`** — `normalizeIssue` now validates via the existing `assertIssue` (unchanged, still throws `TypeError('invalid issue')`), never mutates input, and returns a fresh object with property order `id, title, tags, assignee`. ID/title are trimmed with case preserved; tags are trimmed, lowercased, empties dropped, first-occurrence de-duplicated into a new array; assignee is trimmed/lowercased with empty → `null`, and `null` stays `null`.\n- **`consumers/list.mjs`** — no longer sorts or mutates the input array; validates array-ness (`TypeError('issues must be an array')`) and maps to fresh normalized issues in input order (duplicates kept).\n- **`consumers/search.mjs`** — builds the normalized list first, validates `query` is a string, trims/lowercases it, returns the whole list for empty queries, otherwise filters in original order on normalized title substring or any normalized tag (not IDs/assignees).\n- **`consumers/activity.mjs`** — uses `listIssues`, renders `id|assignee|tags` with `-` for null assignee and comma-joined tags.\n- **`serialize.mjs`** — serializes `listIssues(issues)` so JSON matches list order and normalized property order.\n\nUntouched: `legacy.mjs`, `api.mjs`, `validators.mjs`, fixtures, and the date/paging/console helpers. No tests were executed (no shell available); correctness was checked by reading the code against the stated contract and the existing `public.test.mjs` expectations.",
